From aeeac19a238eca254e974f33d51471ecab2b3293 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: proshiv85-byte <proshiv85@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:23:14 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] WIP: Exynos8895 ACPM DVFS (cpufreq) + TMU thermal

exynos-acpm: load and attach the firmware plugins the 8895 ACPM expects
the host to manage (the kernel DVFS plugin replaces the bootloader one),
add the 8895 match data. clk-acpm: 8895 DVFS clocks; the firmware does
not answer FREQ_GET, so the last rate set is reported.

New exynos8895_tmu driver: read-only, one thermal sensor per TMU probe
with per-probe calibration, left armed by the bootloader.

DT: AP2APM mailbox, APM SRAM, ACPM node, CPU OPP tables from the vendor
cpufreq domains, capacity-dmips-mhz, TMU blocks and thermal zones with
cpufreq cooling. The Cortex-A53 nodes now come first, so the logical
CPU numbers match the labels (boot CPU is cpu@100): 0-3 are the A53s,
4-7 the Mongoose cores.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)
